@startuml
title Full System - Sequence Diagram
autonumber

actor User <<Visitor>>
actor "Registered User" as RegisteredUser <<RegisteredUser>>
actor Admin <<Administrator>>
participant "Postman / API Client" as Client
participant "Massage Reservation API" as API <<APIBoundary>>
participant "Authentication Middleware" as Auth
participant "Authentication Controller" as AuthController
participant "Shop Controller" as ShopController
participant "Reservation Controller" as ReservationController
participant "Rating Controller" as RatingController
participant "Closing Date Controller" as ClosingDateController
database "MongoDB" as DB <<PersistentStore>>
participant "Email Worker" as EmailWorker <<ExternalService>>
actor "Email Provider" as EmailProvider <<EmailProvider>>

== Registration and welcome coupon ==
User -> Client: Submit name, telephone, email, password
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/register
API -> AuthController: register
AuthController -> DB: Create user (password hashed)
DB --> AuthController: New user
AuthController --> API: User details and JWT
AuthController ->> EmailWorker: Generate coupon and send welcome email
EmailWorker -> DB: Create unique promotional coupon
DB --> EmailWorker: Coupon code and expiry
EmailWorker -> EmailProvider: Send welcome email with promo code
EmailProvider --> EmailWorker: Delivery result
API --> Client: Registration successful
Client --> User: Show account and token

== Log in and log out ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Enter email and password
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/login
API -> AuthController: login
AuthController -> DB: Find user and password hash
DB --> AuthController: User record
AuthController -> AuthController: Verify password and issue JWT
AuthController --> API: Access token
API --> Client: Login successful

RegisteredUser -> Client: Log out
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/auth/logout\n(Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth -> DB: Find user and check token version
DB --> Auth: Authenticated user
Auth --> API: Continue
API -> AuthController: logout
AuthController -> DB: Increment tokenVersion
DB --> AuthController: Session revoked
AuthController --> API: Logout successful
API --> Client: Clear cookie and confirm

== Password reset with OTP ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Request password reset by email
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password
API -> AuthController: forgotPassword
AuthController -> DB: Find user; store OTP hash and expiry
DB --> AuthController: Reset request recorded
AuthController ->> EmailWorker: Send reset OTP
EmailWorker -> EmailProvider: Deliver OTP to registered email
EmailProvider --> EmailWorker: Delivery result
AuthController --> API: Generic reset response
API --> Client: Reset instructions

RegisteredUser -> Client: Submit email and OTP
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/verify-otp
API -> AuthController: verifyResetOtp
AuthController -> DB: Verify OTP hash, expiry, and attempts
alt OTP is valid
    DB --> AuthController: Consume OTP; save reset-token hash
    AuthController --> API: Reset token
    API --> Client: Verification successful
    RegisteredUser -> Client: Submit reset token and matching passwords
    Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password
    API -> AuthController: resetPassword
    AuthController -> DB: Set password hash; consume token;\nrevoke existing sessions
    DB --> AuthController: Password changed
    AuthController --> API: Reset successful
    API --> Client: Ask user to log in again
else OTP is invalid or expired
    DB --> AuthController: Verification failed
    AuthController --> API: Invalid or expired OTP
    API --> Client: Show error
end

== Shop information ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: View all shops
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/shops
API -> ShopController: getShops
ShopController -> DB: Read all shop information
DB --> ShopController: Shop names, addresses, phones,\nopening and closing times
ShopController --> API: Shop list
API --> Client: 200 OK

Admin -> Client: Create or edit shop information
Client -> API: POST or PUT /api/v1/shops
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth -> DB: Find admin and check token version
DB --> Auth: Admin account
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ShopController: createShop or updateShop
ShopController -> DB: Save shop information
DB --> ShopController: Created or updated shop
ShopController --> API: Shop result
API --> Client: 201 Created or 200 OK

== Create reservation and notify admin ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Select shop, date, and start time
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/reservations\n(Bearer token, shopId, date, startTime)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth -> DB: Find user and check token version
DB --> Auth: Authenticated user
Auth --> API: Continue as registered user
API -> ReservationController: createReservation
ReservationController -> DB: Check shop and operating hours
DB --> ReservationController: Shop details
ReservationController -> DB: Check special closing date
DB --> ReservationController: Shop open on selected date
ReservationController -> DB: Start transaction; count confirmed bookings
alt User has fewer than 3 active reservations
    DB --> ReservationController: Reservation limit not reached
    ReservationController -> DB: Create confirmed reservation and commit
    DB --> ReservationController: Saved reservation
    ReservationController ->> EmailWorker: Notify admins after commit
    EmailWorker -> DB: Find admin email addresses
    DB --> EmailWorker: Admin recipients
    EmailWorker -> EmailProvider: Send booking notification
    EmailProvider --> EmailWorker: Delivery result
    ReservationController --> API: 201 Created
    API --> Client: Reservation details
else User already has 3 active reservations
    DB --> ReservationController: Reservation limit reached
    ReservationController --> API: 400 Reservation limit reached
    API --> Client: Show limit error
end

== View and manage reservations ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: View own reservations
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/reservations\n(Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> ReservationController: getMyReservations
ReservationController -> DB: Find reservations for current user
DB --> ReservationController: Owner's reservations
ReservationController --> API: Reservation list
API --> Client: 200 OK

RegisteredUser -> Client: Edit or delete own reservation
Client -> API: PUT or DELETE /api/v1/reservations/{id}
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> ReservationController: updateReservation or deleteReservation
ReservationController -> DB: Apply operation only to owner's reservation
DB --> ReservationController: Operation result
ReservationController --> API: Updated/deleted reservation or error
API --> Client: Result

Admin -> Client: View, edit, or delete any reservation
Client -> API: GET, PUT, or DELETE /api/v1/reservations[/{id}]
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ReservationController: Admin reservation operation
ReservationController -> DB: Read or modify any reservation
DB --> ReservationController: Reservation result
ReservationController --> API: Result
API --> Client: Result

== Update reservation status ==
alt Registered user changes own status
    RegisteredUser -> Client: Set status to completed or cancelled
    Client -> API: PATCH /api/v1/reservations/{id}/status
    API -> Auth: Verify JWT
    Auth --> API: Authenticated user
    API -> ReservationController: updateReservationStatus
    ReservationController -> DB: Update owned confirmed reservation
    DB --> ReservationController: Updated status
else Admin changes any reservation status
    Admin -> Client: Set status to completed or cancelled
    Client -> API: PATCH /api/v1/reservations/{id}/status
    API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
    Auth --> API: Continue as admin
    API -> ReservationController: updateReservationStatus
    ReservationController -> DB: Update confirmed reservation
    DB --> ReservationController: Updated status
end
note over ReservationController
    Status changes have no time-based validation.
end note

== Submit and view ratings ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Submit 1-5 star rating for completed reservation
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/reservations/{id}/rating
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> RatingController: createRating
RatingController -> DB: Check ownership and completed status
DB --> RatingController: Eligible reservation
RatingController -> DB: Insert unique rating
DB --> RatingController: Saved rating
RatingController --> API: 201 Created
API --> Client: Rating confirmation

RegisteredUser -> Client: View all ratings
Admin -> Client: View all ratings
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/ratings
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user or admin
API -> RatingController: getRatings
RatingController -> DB: Read ratings and shop/user details
DB --> RatingController: Rating list
RatingController --> API: Ratings
API --> Client: 200 OK

== Manage special closing dates ==
Admin -> Client: Create closing date for a shop
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/shops/{shopId}/closing-dates
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ClosingDateController: createClosingDate
ClosingDateController -> DB: Validate shop and save date
DB --> ClosingDateController: Closing date
ClosingDateController --> API: 201 Created
API --> Client: Closing date details

Admin -> Client: View closing dates for a shop
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/shops/{shopId}/closing-dates
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ClosingDateController: getClosingDates
ClosingDateController -> DB: Read dates for shop
DB --> ClosingDateController: Closing-date list
ClosingDateController --> API: List
API --> Client: 200 OK

Admin -> Client: Update or delete closing date
Client -> API: PUT or DELETE /api/v1/closing-dates/{id}
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ClosingDateController: updateClosingDate or deleteClosingDate
ClosingDateController -> DB: Update or delete closing date
DB --> ClosingDateController: Operation result
ClosingDateController --> API: Result
API --> Client: 200 OK or error

note over Client, API
    The API can be exercised with Postman.
    The 3-second performance target is a non-functional requirement,
    not a timing guarantee shown by this interaction diagram.
end note
@enduml
